<item>
            <title>[LU-20912] LFSCK: EC dangling repair must not zero-fill OST objects</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20912</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;LFSCK repairs a dangling LOV-EA reference by creating an all-zero OST object. This is&#160;wrong for EC components:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1. Missing data stripe: the object then &quot;exists&quot; and reads as zeros, so the client&apos;s read-time EC recovery is never triggered,&lt;br/&gt;
    but if left absent, the read fails and EC reconstructs the real data from parity.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Missing parity stripe: all-zero is an invalid parity value and corrupts later recovery.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;For any EC component, do not create the missing object and leave a missing data stripe absent (let CIT_EC_RD recover it);&lt;br/&gt;
for a missing parity stripe set LCME_FL_STALE so lfs mirror resync recomputes it. If lost stripes in a raid set exceed cstripe_count, report only.  LFSCK must not do the data reconstruction itself (metadata-only). Non-EC files keep the current zero-fill behavior.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
